      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The presence in the same clinical case of diffuse coronary artery ectasia and multiple congenital coronary artery fistulae draining into the left ventricle is a very rare condition. Herein we report the 20-year follow-up of an 85-year old woman, in order to show that the long-term prognosis in such a double disorder is good."},
